# lf134, the sparrow-feeding farmhand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf134
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_ludo_oakholt
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the sparrow-feeding farmhand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk feeds_the_sparrows
likes warm_bread dancing market_bustle warm_rain
dislikes bad_manners rats
fears another winter with no letter from faraway kin a rat taking the grain stores
hopes a letter bearing familiar handwriting a festival dance with family
topics work +0.5 home +0.4 pastimes +0.3 family +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=wry refuse=quiet tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works the #field# at #self.workplace#, shares #bread# with #sparrows#, and watches for a #letter# from far away.

words
oath! = By the seed sack | By the barn door
saying! = Even sparrows find their way home | Rain waits for no harvester
field = field | ploughed field
fields = fields | open fields
farm = farm | Longmead farm
farmhand = farmhand | field hand
soil = soil | dark soil
seed = seed | spring seed
seeds = seeds | saved seeds
sack = sack | grain sack
sacks = sacks | grain sacks
grain = grain | ripe grain
wheat = wheat | standing wheat
barley = barley | cut barley
oat = oat | dry oat
crop = crop | field crop
crops = crops | summer crops
harvest = harvest | late harvest
row = row | seeded row
rows = rows | straight rows
hoe = hoe | worn hoe
spade = spade | iron spade
scythe = scythe | sharp scythe
blade = blade | field blade
barn = barn | Longmead barn
granary = granary | Longmead granary
loft = loft | granary loft
bin = bin | grain bin
bins = bins | grain bins
floor = floor | barn floor
roof = roof | sound roof
boot = boot | worn boot
boots = boots | muddy boots
door = door | barn door
gate = gate | farm gate
fence = fence | field fence
post = post | fence post
wood = wood | dry wood
cart = cart | grain cart
wagon = wagon | farm wagon
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
road = road | market road
market = market | town market
stall = stall | bread stall
crowd = crowd | market crowd
bustle = bustle | market bustle
coin = coin | hard coin
wage = wage | small wage
merchant = merchant | town merchant
bread = bread | warm bread
crust = crust | bread crust
loaf = loaf | fresh loaf
oven = oven | hot oven
meal = meal | midday meal
table = table | kitchen table
home = home | shared home
hearth = hearth | kitchen hearth
window = window | small window
letter = letter | folded letter
letters = letters | distant letters
writing = writing | familiar writing
family = family | distant family
kin = kin | faraway kin
spouse = spouse | dear spouse
friend = friend | old friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
sparrow = sparrow | small sparrow
sparrows = sparrows | roof sparrows
bird = bird | field bird
birds = birds | wild birds
crumb = crumb | bread crumb
crumbs = crumbs | spare crumbs
rat = rat | hungry rat
rats = rats | granary rats
trap = trap | rat trap
festival = festival | harvest festival
dance = dance | festival dance
music = music | fiddle music
fiddle = fiddle | festival fiddle
rain = rain | warm rain
cloud = cloud | passing cloud
sun = sun | late sun
spring = spring | early spring
summer = summer | dry summer
autumn = autumn | wet autumn
winter = winter | long winter
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | slow evening
night = night | quiet night
day = day | working day
hour = hour | long hour
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | calloused hands
work = work | field work
rest = rest | deserved rest
manners = manners | table manners
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
watch = watch | town watch
city = city | distant city
house = house | great house
houses = houses | great houses

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : A #city# has no room to leave #crumbs# for #sparrows#. | I prefer the #field# after #rain#.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : I wait at the #dance# until the #fiddle# catches me. | #self.spouse# can pull me onto the #floor#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I cut #wheat# in the shadow of a great #house#. | The folk inside never lift a #sack#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A #merchant# asks more for one #loaf# than a day's #wage# allows. | The #grain# left our own #field#.
opinion @1 road for 1 : The #road# will take a person to faraway #kin#. | It can bring a #letter# back too.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A #stranger# may need #bread#. | I still count the #sacks# after a visit.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #bins# seem emptier each #winter#. | The work grows longer for the same #coin#.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The #watch# passes the #gate# on its round. | It rarely comes through the #field#.
line @1 greet : #greet#. A half-planted #row# calls me back. | #greet#. Mind the #sparrows# at your feet.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I saved a #crust# for the #birds#. | Come by after the #work# is done.
line @1 greet.return : The #field# is where you left it. | I am still waiting for that #letter#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come close to the #hearth#. | There is #bread# enough at our #table#.
line @1 again.open : We had left the #seed# by the #gate#. | You were asking about my faraway #kin#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #hoe# is waiting. | Step around the newly seeded #rows#.
line @1 farewell.return : If a #letter# arrives, I will be here. | Another #dance# may come around.
line @1 react.news : Let me set down this #sack#. | Is it from beyond the #road#?
line @1 react.news.new : I have heard no word of that while working the #field#. | Who brought the word to #market#?
line @1 react.news.known : Someone mentioned it near the #granary#. | Your account gives it a different end.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Who actually watched that #wagon# pass? | The #road# has carried false reports before.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Sit at the #table# while I bring #bread#. | I will stay at the #table# and hear you out.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That calls for fresh #bread#. | There may even be a #dance# tonight.
line @1 answer.how : The #rows# are coming along. | Better after that warm #rain#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am turning this #soil# before it dries. | These #sacks# need carrying to the #loft#.
line @1 ask.how : What did you see along the #road#? | Did you find a good #meal# today?
line @1 sympathise : Take some #bread# for the walk. | I can sit with you when the #row# is finished.
line @1 reassure : We have #seed# set aside for another #spring#. | I will help mend that #fence#.
line @1 decline : These wet #rows# need one more turn before I go. | The #granary# needs its #bins# checked first.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand; we will leave that #gate# closed. | Then we can bring the #cart# through.
line @1 thank : The #sacks# were easier with another pair of #hands#. | You brought word from the #road# when I needed it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had spare #bread# anyway. | The #cart# was going past your #home#.
line @1 preclose : The #sparrows# will be looking for #crumbs#. | I need to bring this #hoe# indoors.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You would plant the #seed# upside down if it could be done. | Your #dance# needs a wider #floor#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #grain# is dry. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the #fence#.
line @1 give.advice : Keep #bread# covered when the #rats# are near. | Let the #soil# settle after a warm #rain#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Do not take the #market# #road# alone tonight. | Keep your #coin# inside your #boot#.
scene sparrow_crumbs
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave #crumbs# on the #window# ledge for the #sparrows#. | They wait for me before #morning# work.
b : Do they come every day? | Does your wife mind?
a : Except in hard #rain#. | #self.spouse# leaves some too.

scene far_letters
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #kin# live beyond the #city# and never send #letters#. | I still look at the #road# when the post comes.
b : Have you written first? | Will you visit?
a : Several times. | When the #harvest# is through.

scene grain_sacks
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #grain# #sacks# feel heavier after a full #day# in the #field#. | We stack them by the #granary# #door#.
b : How many today? | Who helps?
a : Enough for a sore back. | The other #hands#.

scene seed_rows
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I mark a straight #row# with a stretched cord. | The #seed# needs room to grow.
b : Does it stay straight? | Who taught you?
a : Near enough. | An old #farmhand#.

scene rat_trap
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #rat# left a trail of #grain# by the #bin#. | I moved the #trap# under the #loft# steps.
b : Did you catch it? | Are there more?
a : One. | Always more.

scene warm_loaf
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first #loaf# out of the #oven# never reaches the #market#. | We cut it at the #table#.
b : Do you keep a piece? | Is it worth waiting?
a : A thick #crust#. | Every time.

scene festival_edge
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I stand near the #festival# #music# until I know the tune. | Then #self.spouse# takes my #hand#.
b : Do you dance well? | Do you like it?
a : Well enough to return. | More than I admit.

scene market_noise
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #market# #bustle# wakes me up after a quiet #field#. | I buy #bread# and make for the #field# once the sellers start shouting.
b : Do you go often? | Do you sell anything?
a : When we need supplies. | The #grain# goes with others.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A warm #rain# softens the #soil# without washing the #seed# away. | I work the #rows# while I can.
b : Does it last? | Is it your favourite weather?
a : Never long enough. | For planting, yes.

scene fence_post
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #fence# by the #road# has a leaning #post#. | I set it straight whenever I pass.
b : Does it hold? | Why keep doing it?
a : For a while. | The #crop# needs guarding.

scene scythe_edge
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sharpen the #scythe# before the #sun# reaches the #barn#. | A dull #blade# wastes both time and #wheat#.
b : Can I see it? | Who taught you?
a : After I cover it. | My first #farmhand#.

scene dry_loft
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #loft# keeps the #grain# out of #rain#. | I check the #roof# after each storm.
b : Any leaks? | What if it does leak?
a : One near the #door#. | Move the #sacks#.

scene late_window
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sit by the #window# after the #evening# meal. | Sometimes a traveller passes with a #letter#.
b : Do you ask them? | Is that tiring?
a : Only if they stop. | A little.

scene table_manners
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A guest can eat every #crumb# and still leave the #table# pleasantly. | Bad #manners# spoil a good #loaf#.
b : What do you say? | Is it common?
a : I pass the #bread# once. | Common enough.

scene field_rest
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take my rest where the #field# meets the #road#. | The #sparrows# come down when I open my #meal#.
b : Do they eat from your hand? | Do you rest long?
a : Sometimes. | Until the #sun# moves.

scene winter_seed
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One #winter# we used the last dry #seed# to start the #spring# rows. | I remember counting each #sack#.
b : Did it grow? | Were you afraid?
a : Enough to fill a #bin#. | I was.

scene household_hands
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #home# has several working #hands# under one #roof#. | A warm #hearth# matters more than a wide #floor#.
b : Is it crowded? | Do you stay there?
a : At #meal# time. | For now.

story empty_post [topic=family self.age>=18]
  : I saw the post come through the #gate# after a long #winter#.
  : None of the #letters# held my family's #writing#.
  ask : Did you write again?
  b : A hard wait.
  : I did, and kept a little hope for #spring#.

story rain_planting [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : Warm #rain# fell while we still had #seed# in the #sacks#.
  : We planted every #row# before dark.
  ask : Did the crop take?
  b : That sounds tiring.
  : It came up green and straight.

story first_dance [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I waited outside the #festival# until the #fiddle# began.
  : #self.spouse# took my #hand# and pulled me across the #floor#.
  ask : Did you dance?
  b : That was kind.
  : Badly, but I asked for another tune.

rule @bark_sparrows
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #sparrows# found my #crumbs#. | There is one on the #fence# again.

rule @bark_grain
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say That #sack# belongs in the #loft#. | Keep the #grain# dry.

rule @bark_letter
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say No #letter# in the post today. | Perhaps the next #wagon# carries one.

rule @bark_dance
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say I know that #fiddle# tune. | The #festival# is soon.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am heading back to the #field#. | #greet#. There is warm #bread# on our #table#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #sparrows# came back this #morning#. | Still no #letter# from my #kin#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work the #fields# at #self.workplace#. | I plant #seed#, carry #sacks#, and keep #rats# from the #grain#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. The #rows# need me. | Come by for the next #dance#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why feed the sparrows? -> birds
node birds
say They stay through the #winter# when other #birds# leave. A few #crumbs# are easy to spare.
free
choice Has your family written? -> letters
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node letters
say No #letter# yet, but I watch the #road# when the post arrives.
choice Back to the field. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #seed# is ready. | #greet#. I must fetch the #hoe#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #barn# is still open. | I will see to the #sparrows#.
